# Security policy

## Reporting

Report suspected vulnerabilities privately to the repository maintainers. Do not include secrets, exploit payloads, personal data, or unredacted production logs in a public issue.

## Required engineering controls

- Treat all external input and agent/tool output as untrusted data.
- Keep credentials out of source, prompts, logs, fixtures, and committed agent configuration.
- Use least-privilege workflow permissions and pinned GitHub Action commit SHAs.
- Update and commit the configured SBOM after dependency changes; CI validates its package identities.
- Use `.agent-standard/waivers.json` only for time-bounded, owned exceptions with a concrete reason.

## Supported versions

Until the project publishes a release policy, only the default branch is supported.
